  "problem": "Consider the inexact differential equation\n\n$$\n(\\frac{5{y}^{2}}{x}+2{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+(5y+2x{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\nIt is known that \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y}-\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x})=\\frac{2}{x}\n$$\n\nwhere the functions $P$ and $Q$ are given by \n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\frac{5{y}^{2}}{x}+2{y}^{3},\\,Q(x,y)=5y+2x{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUse this information to find a suitable integrating factor $I(x)$ and hence find the general solution to the equation.$\\,$ A suitable integrating factor is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is {{field-2}}, where $c$ is a constant.",
